+# Task6 — saved transcript, marks and confirmation
+
+Implemented in `/home/tanren/ama/.worktrees/phase-b-completion`, branch `codex/phase-b-completion-20261023`, review BASE and pre-delivery HEAD `80c878f52c7b748efdcdb64e707d50cf410843b4`. The delivery commit contains this report; its exact ID is supplied in the author handoff. No push or merge. Independent SPEC/quality review and adoption remain root work.
+
+## Delivered behavior
+
+- Complete bounded S → outside-root A → fresh F reader, using the same genuine JdbcTranscriptAuthority/DS/holder/gate/purpose issuer. Both phases retain actual revision/segment/FK parent locks and complete indexed child sets, including empty marks. All content-bearing sets and manifest lengths are admitted before any LONGTEXT transfer. UTF-8 bytes, Unicode scalars, UTF-16 units, copies, response projection, canonical nodes/containers/bytes, ancestry and facts have cumulative finite admission; selected full text is never clipped or paginated. History alone has bounded metadata pages and exclusive lossless revision cursor.
+- Save, marks and restoration create complete immutable WORKING copies with unchanged stable segment identity and original source/input/batch/parent ancestry. Human revisions have no producer task. Actual CAS/fence/search revision advances exactly once, confirmations clear, generation debt is set, audit and outbox share the transaction and flush last. Full persisted readback is compared before acceptance.
+- `hashDraft` hashes persisted WORKING without fake confirmation IDs/rows/hashes. It shares the existing canonical algorithm and original four-archive closure with confirmed hashing. Old independent confirmed/manual goldens remain unchanged. First confirmation persists real UUID/hash; unchanged current confirmation reuses it without advancing revision. A fresh request can reattach that same immutable confirmation after another genuine intake cleared its pointer; an old receipt never reattaches.
+- Current, exact owner history, complete marks, confirmations and source routes are real HTTP endpoints with strict streaming 8 MiB request envelope, lossless tokens, complete segment/mark lists, explicit error codes and private no-store on success and error. OpenAPI and mechanically regenerated TypeScript cover these endpoints. No Web UI or model runtime was added.
+- Owner historical stored-text inspection verifies complete retained provenance while independently reporting source-byte eligibility. Effective members receive only current confirmed projection and cannot inspect history or mutate. Platform role does not grant content access. Fresh B03 authorization precedes replay return. Missing/corrupt provenance never becomes an authorization bypass.
+- Accepted-result lookup occurs before current operational budgets/profiles/correction guards. After an ordinary S prerequisite/budget failure, exactly one new lookup can return a concurrently accepted identity. The named allowlist excludes corruption, malformed input, cancellation and authorization failure. F rechecks full facts and current guards; nonordinary A corruption takes precedence over a concurrent winner.
+- Actual disabled correction component has trusted matching selected/declaration/version, empty actual provider inventory, unique boot qualification and private component identity. No PENDING count or empty installed reader. Future candidate/publication declarations and inventories fail closed; authentic held-fact integration seams exist, but Task10/11 implementations remain uninstalled.
+
+## Qualification and scope
+
+Root pin `task-06-concrete-runtime-pin-20261024.json` SHA `922ef12101c4f7111e89a1ca2ca86ca84c2c64b74999d104254a1917ccd940a2`, additive refresh `task-06-concrete-runtime-pin-refresh-01-20261024.json` SHA `23221a61c7bebb7d57be2d4855b1a6d86ffa57edc7b944d6ff4a2eb86c604f8a` authorize only this controlled local test combination. They are offline evidence; runtime never reads Git or approval files.
+
+Configured acquisition UTF-8/scalars/UTF-16 are 16 Mi each; actual effective UTF-8/scalars are **1 Mi** each because of the shared archive budget. UTF-16 is independently 16 Mi units; per-text UTF-8 262144 bytes and UTF-16 65536 units; copies 64 Mi bytes/units; request 8 MiB and response 32 MiB; ancestry depth128/nodes256/tasks64. Four original archives total1884 bytes, index SHA `c6e3b29cedbdc5234f368fa6d1f7152442c95f56b0caaf52bc8019bafea13e9d`; original parser65536 bytes/65536 UTF-16/2048 segments and canonical16777216 bytes/depth32/nodes1000000/string2097152/container250000 remain binding minima. Full configured/effective quantities, references, manifests and actual observations are in the candidate/additive manifests and pipeline receipts. Independent ceilings are conservative; no simultaneous maximum payload or memory/capacity claim.
